## 6. What checked out

Independently re-verified by hand and **correct**: all five Table 2 witnesses (16/47, 17/47, 29/80, 4/11, 1793/5000) with their stated σ and opposite-slope binding; the 7/22 center class; the 607/1792 negative control (minimiser σ = 89/896); the balance family at k=20 and k=35; all four binding pair forms at the harmonic argmax and all three at m=12; the weight identity, both denominator archetypes, 94·(16/47)=32 and 188·(17/47)=68; the h\* polynomials for n=3,4,5 and the volume identity at n=10 (19,958,400 = 9!·55; 23,587,200 = 9!·65); the Newton floors and the n≈26 crossing; and every leaf/split count (190,295−95,147 = 95,148; 782,255−391,127 = 391,128; the five prune classes sum to 391,128). Repo-side figures I cross-checked also match: 222 leaves at m=16, 782,255/0 and 190,295/0, 45-dp Sturm, Spearman +0.32/−0.31, and the m=9 ordering 455/1269 ≈ 0.358550 < 1793/5000 = 0.358600 < 0.358639.

**The mathematics is sound. The release engineering and the paper↔repo number reconciliation are not.**

